# libcss: -macsurf-grid parses a raw CSS track list (patch 340, with 340-netsurf)
# Generated 2026-10-30
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 339)
#
# When css_rewrite cannot expand a var() in grid-template-columns, it now
# emits `-macsurf-grid: var(...)` (340-netsurf), so at cascade time the
# -macsurf-grid parser receives the substituted CSS track list (MDN:
# `[full-start sidebar-start] minmax(15rem,1fr) [...] 2rem ...`).
#
#  - p_macsurf_grid.c: a value starting with '[' or a function token goes
#    to css__parse_grid_template_columns() (until now dead code, declared
#    in properties.h for this).
#  - p_grid_template_columns.c, that raw parser: rem/em lengths at the
#    16px root font (they were taken as px: 15rem became 15px).
#    minmax(<length>, <fr>) packs the floor-plus-fr kind (5), and
#    minmax(0, <length>) packs the grows-toward kind (9, patch 337).
#    Before, minmax kept one bound as a plain track.
